  "wholeLocalCheckpoint": 180,
  "verificationScope": "Let K be a field and S a commutative K-algebra graded by B indexed over the natural numbers. For every positive integer q, Proj of this original grading is isomorphic as a scheme to Proj of the subalgebra graded by the original degree-qn pieces. The morphisms are glued on common positive homogeneous denominators. On each affine chart they are induced by the exact degree-zero fraction maps; both restriction formulas and both inverse identities are verified. This identifies the schemes and their structure sheaves as part of the scheme isomorphism. The comparison of the original coefficient sheaf, identification of fixed C_L with cut-dependent C_H, and the same normalized geometric trace remain open. Original Lemmas 4.1 and 4.2 and the main theorem remain open. Whole local checkpoint 180.",
